        content: `You build a dashboard with **three pivots**: revenue by region, units by category, and top-10 customers. A user wants to filter all three by **Year**.

**Wrong way.** Insert three Year slicers — users click three times, mistakes happen.

**Right way.** Insert **one** slicer from any pivot. Right-click the slicer → **Report Connections** (older versions: **PivotTable Connections**). A dialog lists every pivot in the workbook. **Check all three.** Now one click on **2024** filters all three pivots simultaneously.

**The naming payoff.** That dialog shows pivot names. If you renamed them **pvt_RevByRegion**, **pvt_UnitsByCategory**, **pvt_TopCustomers**, you instantly know what to check. If they're **PivotTable1/4/9**, you're guessing. The **rename** step pays off here — and in every macro, slicer, and reference for the life of the workbook.`,
