        type: "intro",
        title: "Shape Your Data First",
        content: `Raw data rarely arrives clean. Before you can analyze it, you need to **remove junk columns**, **filter out irrelevant rows**, **drop duplicates**, and **sort** what remains. Power Query gives you a ribbon full of point-and-click tools to do exactly this — and every action becomes a **repeatable step**.

In this lesson you'll master four core transforms: **Remove Columns** (and the safer **Remove Other Columns**), **Remove Duplicates** (with a critical gotcha about selection), **Filter Rows** (text, number, date), and **Sort** (single and multi-column). You'll also learn the **Keep Rows** family — handy for previewing samples or trimming report footers.

These transforms run automatically every refresh. Set them up once, and your data arrives **pre-shaped** every time.`,
