        content: `Try this end-to-end. You have **Customers.xlsx** with 50 columns and ~25,000 rows. Your goal: a Top 10 list by lifetime spend, current customers only.

**1.** Get Data → Excel → Customers.xlsx → Transform Data.

**2.** Ctrl-click **CustomerID**, **Name**, **Status**, **LifetimeSpend** → right-click → **Remove Other Columns**.

**3.** Click the **Status** dropdown → uncheck "Inactive" and "Churned" → OK. (Or right-click → Text Filters → Equals "Active".)

**4.** Click the **LifetimeSpend** column header → **Sort Descending**.

**5.** Home tab → **Keep Rows → Keep Top Rows** → enter **10**.

**6.** Right-click **CustomerID** → **Remove Duplicates** (paranoid check).

**7.** Close & Load to a table.

Refresh next month — same query, same 4 columns, same Top 10 logic, **new data**. That's the Power Query payoff: build once, refresh forever. Bonus: change the **10** in step 5 to **25** and the whole report scales instantly.`,
