        type: "example",
        title: "A Real Tuning Session",
        content: `**Before:** Sales dashboard takes 14 seconds to load.

**Step 1 — Record.** View → Performance Analyzer → Start → click each slicer once → Stop. Results:
- **Customer scatter:** 6.4s (visual display heavy)
- **Sales by Region bar:** 8.2s (DAX query heavy)
- **YTD KPI card:** 0.07s (fine)

**Step 2 — Fix the bar chart.** The measure was \`Sales by Region = CALCULATE(SUM(Sales[Amount]), FILTER(Sales, Sales[Region] = MAX(Region[Name])))\`. The **FILTER(Sales, ...)** scanned 22M rows. Rewrote to \`CALCULATE(SUM(Sales[Amount]))\` — context transition handles the filter for free. Time: **8.2s → 0.4s**.

**Step 3 — Fix the scatter.** 250k customer dots. Added a **Top N filter** to show only top 1000 by revenue. Time: **6.4s → 0.6s**.

**Step 4 — Fix the model.** Spotted **bidirectional** filter on Customer → Sales. Not needed; switched to **single-direction**. Saved 200ms across all visuals.

**Step 5 — Cardinality.** Dropped \`Sales[TransactionID]\` (28M unique values, never displayed). Model size dropped from **480MB → 210MB**, refresh got 40% faster.

**After:** Dashboard loads in **1.1 seconds**.`,
