          svg: `<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 1100 1100"><rect width="1100" height="1100" fill="#1a1a2e"/><text x="550" y="60" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffd700" font-size="34" font-weight="bold">Retail-Prod Workspace on F64</text><rect x="80" y="120" width="940" height="80" fill="#0ea5e9" rx="10"/><text x="550" y="170" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffffff" font-size="24" font-weight="bold">1. Data Factory Pipeline -&gt; S3 POS files -&gt; Lakehouse</text><polygon points="540,210 560,210 550,250" fill="#ffd700"/><rect x="80" y="260" width="940" height="80" fill="#ffd700" rx="10"/><text x="550" y="310" text-anchor="middle" fill="#1a1a2e" font-size="24" font-weight="bold">2. Spark Notebook -&gt; dedupe + join + curated tables</text><polygon points="540,350 560,350 550,390" fill="#ffd700"/><rect x="80" y="400" width="940" height="80" fill="#10b981" rx="10"/><text x="550" y="450" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffffff" font-size="24" font-weight="bold">3. Direct Lake Semantic Model on Lakehouse</text><polygon points="540,490 560,490 550,530" fill="#ffd700"/><rect x="80" y="540" width="940" height="80" fill="#ec4899" rx="10"/><text x="550" y="590" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffffff" font-size="24" font-weight="bold">4. Power BI Reports -&gt; sub-second visuals</text><rect x="80" y="660" width="940" height="100" fill="#6366f1" rx="10"/><text x="550" y="710" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffffff" font-size="22" font-weight="bold">All layers share OneLake storage</text><text x="550" y="740" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffd700" font-size="18">no data copies between workloads</text><rect x="100" y="800" width="900" height="260" fill="#ffd700" rx="12" opacity="0.2"/><text x="550" y="850" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffd700" font-size="28" font-weight="bold">Capacity Economics</text><text x="140" y="910" fill="#ffffff" font-size="20">- F64 runs Mon-Fri 6 AM to 6 PM</text><text x="140" y="950" fill="#ffffff" font-size="20">- Paused weekends + overnight</text><text x="140" y="990" fill="#ffffff" font-size="20">- ~60 paid hours/week vs 168 always-on</text><text x="140" y="1030" fill="#10b981" font-size="22" font-weight="bold">~65% capacity cost savings vs legacy Premium</text></svg>`,
          caption: "Pipelines, Spark, model, and reports run on one F-SKU — pause for weekends to save."
