      {
        type: "concept",
        title: "App Owns Data vs User Owns Data",
        content: `Embedded Power BI splits into **two licensing models** — get this wrong and you'll either bankrupt the project or fail compliance.

**Embed for your organization ("User Owns Data"):** every viewer must have a **Power BI Pro license** of their own. The app uses **OAuth on behalf of the signed-in user** to call the Power BI REST API. Best for **internal apps**: your accountants viewing custom-branded finance dashboards inside your finance portal.

**Embed for your customers ("App Owns Data"):** customers **don't have Power BI accounts**. The app uses a **service principal** (or master user) to authenticate to Power BI, then generates a **short-lived embed token** (JWT, usually 1 hour) and passes it to the JavaScript SDK. The capacity is licensed via **Power BI Embedded (A-SKU)** or **Fabric F-SKU** — billed to the **ISV**, not the end users. Best for **SaaS products**: your customers see charts inside your product, none the wiser that Power BI is the engine.

Same engine, two billing models. Choose based on **who the viewer is**, not technical preference.`,
        visual: {
          type: "diagram",
          svg: `<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 1100 1100"><rect width="1100" height="1100" fill="#1a1a2e"/><text x="550" y="60" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffd700" font-size="34" font-weight="bold">Two Embedding Models</text><rect x="60" y="120" width="490" height="500" fill="#0ea5e9" rx="12"/><text x="305" y="170" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffffff" font-size="26" font-weight="bold">User Owns Data</text><text x="305" y="205" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffd700" font-size="18">("Embed for your organization")</text><text x="80" y="260" fill="#ffffff" font-size="20" font-weight="bold">Viewer:</text><text x="80" y="290" fill="#ffffff" font-size="18">Internal employee with Pro license</text><text x="80" y="340" fill="#ffffff" font-size="20" font-weight="bold">Auth:</text><text x="80" y="370" fill="#ffffff" font-size="18">OAuth on behalf of the user</text><text x="80" y="420" fill="#ffffff" font-size="20" font-weight="bold">Licensing:</text><text x="80" y="450" fill="#ffffff" font-size="18">Each user buys Pro themselves</text><text x="80" y="500" fill="#ffffff" font-size="20" font-weight="bold">Best for:</text><text x="80" y="530" fill="#ffffff" font-size="18">Internal portals, intranet apps</text><text x="80" y="580" fill="#10b981" font-size="20" font-weight="bold">Cost stays in IT budget</text><rect x="570" y="120" width="490" height="500" fill="#8b5cf6" rx="12"/><text x="815" y="170" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffffff" font-size="26" font-weight="bold">App Owns Data</text><text x="815" y="205" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffd700" font-size="18">("Embed for your customers")</text><text x="590" y="260" fill="#ffffff" font-size="20" font-weight="bold">Viewer:</text><text x="590" y="290" fill="#ffffff" font-size="18">External customer, NO PBI account</text><text x="590" y="340" fill="#ffffff" font-size="20" font-weight="bold">Auth:</text><text x="590" y="370" fill="#ffffff" font-size="18">Service principal -&gt; embed token</text><text x="590" y="420" fill="#ffffff" font-size="20" font-weight="bold">Licensing:</text><text x="590" y="450" fill="#ffffff" font-size="18">ISV buys A-SKU or F-SKU capacity</text><text x="590" y="500" fill="#ffffff" font-size="20" font-weight="bold">Best for:</text><text x="590" y="530" fill="#ffffff" font-size="18">SaaS products, public dashboards</text><text x="590" y="580" fill="#10b981" font-size="20" font-weight="bold">Cost scales with ISV usage</text><rect x="80" y="660" width="940" height="80" fill="#ffd700" rx="10"/><text x="550" y="710" text-anchor="middle" fill="#1a1a2e" font-size="22" font-weight="bold">Same engine. Same RLS. Different billing &amp; auth.</text><rect x="100" y="770" width="900" height="290" fill="#6366f1" rx="12" opacity="0.25"/><text x="550" y="820" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffd700" font-size="26" font-weight="bold">Quick Decision Rule</text><text x="140" y="880" fill="#ffffff" font-size="20">Does each viewer already have a Power BI Pro license?</text><text x="180" y="930" fill="#10b981" font-size="20" font-weight="bold">YES -&gt; User Owns Data</text><text x="180" y="970" fill="#ec4899" font-size="20" font-weight="bold">NO  -&gt; App Owns Data</text><text x="140" y="1030" fill="#ffffff" font-size="18">(External customers almost always = App Owns Data)</text></svg>`,
          caption: "Internal users with Pro = User Owns Data. External customers without accounts = App Owns Data."
        }
      },
      {
        type: "example",
        title: "Embedding a Sales Dashboard in a SaaS App",
        content: `**Scenario:** Acme HQ sells a CRM SaaS product. Customers want a **Sales Pipeline** dashboard inside the CRM — branded as Acme HQ, no Power BI logos visible.

**Architecture (App Owns Data):**

**1. Capacity.** Acme HQ provisions a **Fabric F8** dedicated to embedded workloads.

**2. Service principal.** A registered Azure AD application is granted **workspace contributor** access. No human user account involved.

**3. Token generation.** When a customer signs into the CRM, the backend (Node.js) calls Power BI REST: \`POST /v1.0/myorg/GenerateToken\` with the report ID, the **service principal credential**, and a **rowLevelSecurity username** matching the customer's tenant.

**4. Render.** The frontend uses the **powerbi-client-react** SDK with the returned token + embed URL. The dashboard appears as a div inside the CRM page.

**5. RLS.** Each customer only sees their own pipeline because the token's RLS identity restricts data.

Customers see Acme HQ branding. They never know Power BI exists.`,
        visual: {
          type: "diagram",
          svg: `<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 1100 1100"><rect width="1100" height="1100" fill="#1a1a2e"/><text x="550" y="60" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffd700" font-size="32" font-weight="bold">App Owns Data: Embed Token Flow</text><rect x="80" y="120" width="280" height="100" fill="#0ea5e9" rx="10"/><text x="220" y="165" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffffff" font-size="20" font-weight="bold">Customer Browser</text><text x="220" y="195" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffffff" font-size="16">CRM page loads</text><polygon points="360,165 410,160 410,175" fill="#ffd700"/><rect x="420" y="120" width="280" height="100" fill="#6366f1" rx="10"/><text x="560" y="165" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffffff" font-size="20" font-weight="bold">CRM Backend</text><text x="560" y="195" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffffff" font-size="16">Node.js / .NET</text><polygon points="700,165 750,160 750,175" fill="#ffd700"/><rect x="760" y="120" width="280" height="100" fill="#ec4899" rx="10"/><text x="900" y="165" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffffff" font-size="20" font-weight="bold">Power BI REST</text><text x="900" y="195" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffffff" font-size="16">GenerateToken</text><text x="900" y="260" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffd700" font-size="16">authenticates with</text><text x="900" y="285" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffd700" font-size="16">service principal</text><polygon points="900,310 895,360 905,360" fill="#ffd700"/><rect x="760" y="370" width="280" height="100" fill="#ffd700" rx="10"/><text x="900" y="415" text-anchor="middle" fill="#1a1a2e" font-size="20" font-weight="bold">Embed Token</text><text x="900" y="445" text-anchor="middle" fill="#1a1a2e" font-size="16">JWT, 1-hour TTL</text><polygon points="760,420 710,415 710,430" fill="#ffd700"/><text x="560" y="430" fill="#ffd700" font-size="16" text-anchor="middle">token returned</text><polygon points="420,460 370,465 370,450" fill="#ffd700"/><rect x="80" y="490" width="280" height="100" fill="#10b981" rx="10"/><text x="220" y="535" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffffff" font-size="20" font-weight="bold">powerbi-client SDK</text><text x="220" y="565" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffffff" font-size="16">renders &lt;div&gt;</text><rect x="80" y="630" width="940" height="170" fill="#6366f1" rx="12" opacity="0.3"/><text x="550" y="680" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffd700" font-size="24" font-weight="bold">Token Carries RLS Identity</text><text x="140" y="730" fill="#ffffff" font-size="20">GenerateToken body includes:</text><text x="180" y="765" fill="#10b981" font-size="18">"identities": [{"username": "acme-corp-tenant-id",</text><text x="180" y="790" fill="#10b981" font-size="18">                "roles": ["TenantViewer"]}]</text><rect x="100" y="830" width="900" height="230" fill="#ffd700" rx="12" opacity="0.2"/><text x="550" y="880" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffd700" font-size="26" font-weight="bold">Customer Experience</text><text x="140" y="940" fill="#ffffff" font-size="20">- Sees only their own tenant's pipeline data (RLS)</text><text x="140" y="985" fill="#ffffff" font-size="20">- Acme HQ logo + colors, no Power BI branding</text><text x="140" y="1030" fill="#ffffff" font-size="20">- No login to Power BI required</text></svg>`,
          caption: "Backend service principal mints a short-lived JWT; SDK renders the report inline with RLS scoping."
        }
      },
      {
        type: "quiz",
        title: "Mobile &amp; Embedded Knowledge Check",
        question: "A SaaS company wants to embed Power BI dashboards inside their product so paying customers (who have NO Microsoft accounts) can view tenant-scoped data. Which model and key component fit?",
        options: [
          { text: "Embed for your organization (User Owns Data), each customer buys a Pro license", correct: false },
          { text: "Embed for your customers (App Owns Data), service principal mints an embed token", correct: true },
          { text: "Power BI Mobile app with Intune MDM enforcement for each customer", correct: false },
          { text: "Mobile-optimized layout published as a public dashboard with RLS disabled", correct: false }
        ],
        explanation: `External customers without Power BI accounts is the textbook **App Owns Data** scenario. The ISV provisions a **Power BI Embedded (A-SKU) or Fabric F-SKU** capacity, registers a **service principal** in Azure AD, and the backend calls \`GenerateToken\` to mint a **short-lived JWT embed token** that the frontend SDK uses to render the report. **RLS still applies** — the token carries an identity / role that scopes data to that customer's tenant. User Owns Data would require every customer to buy a Pro license, which is impractical for SaaS. Public dashboards with RLS disabled would leak everyone's data.`,
        visual: {
          type: "diagram",
          svg: `<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 1100 1100"><rect width="1100" height="1100" fill="#1a1a2e"/><text x="550" y="80" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffd700" font-size="36" font-weight="bold">SaaS Embedding Checklist</text><rect x="80" y="160" width="940" height="80" fill="#8b5cf6" rx="10"/><text x="550" y="210" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffffff" font-size="24" font-weight="bold">1. App Owns Data licensing model</text><rect x="80" y="260" width="940" height="80" fill="#0ea5e9" rx="10"/><text x="550" y="310" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffffff" font-size="24" font-weight="bold">2. Capacity: Embedded A-SKU or Fabric F-SKU</text><rect x="80" y="360" width="940" height="80" fill="#10b981" rx="10"/><text x="550" y="410" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffffff" font-size="24" font-weight="bold">3. Azure AD service principal as workspace member</text><rect x="80" y="460" width="940" height="80" fill="#ffd700" rx="10"/><text x="550" y="510" text-anchor="middle" fill="#1a1a2e" font-size="24" font-weight="bold">4. Backend mints embed token via REST API</text><rect x="80" y="560" width="940" height="80" fill="#ec4899" rx="10"/><text x="550" y="610" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffffff" font-size="24" font-weight="bold">5. RLS identity passed in token = tenant scoping</text><rect x="80" y="660" width="940" height="80" fill="#f59e0b" rx="10"/><text x="550" y="710" text-anchor="middle" fill="#1a1a2e" font-size="24" font-weight="bold">6. powerbi-client SDK renders in browser</text><rect x="100" y="780" width="900" height="280" fill="#6366f1" rx="12" opacity="0.25"/><text x="550" y="840" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffd700" font-size="28" font-weight="bold">Common Gotchas</text><text x="140" y="900" fill="#ffffff" font-size="20">- Token TTL is ~1 hour - refresh server-side</text><text x="140" y="950" fill="#ffffff" font-size="20">- RLS must be tested with EACH customer identity</text><text x="140" y="1000" fill="#ffffff" font-size="20">- Q&amp;A, Smart Narratives have limited embed support</text></svg>`,
          caption: "App Owns Data: capacity + service principal + embed token + RLS — the standard SaaS embedding stack."
        }
      },
      {
        type: "application",
        title: "Choosing the Right Surface",
        content: `Pick the right Power BI surface for your audience:

**Internal dashboards for ~50 employees** → publish to the **Service**, share via **App**. Every user gets Pro; native mobile app comes free. Don't embed unless you have a real custom-app need.

**Internal portal with custom branding** → **User Owns Data** embed. Users still need Pro, but the embed lets you wrap reports in your portal's chrome and navigation.

**SaaS product for external customers** → **App Owns Data** embed. Service principal + F-SKU capacity. Plan capacity sizing carefully — embedded workloads consume CUs per render.

**Field staff on phones** → publish to Service, add **mobile-optimized layouts** in Desktop, set up **data alerts** for KPIs (e.g., notify when daily sales drop below threshold). Users install the **Power BI mobile app**.

**Public-facing dashboard (anonymous)** → "Publish to web" or **Fabric Embed for anonymous access** (F64+). Caution: **RLS often can't be enforced** for anonymous viewers — only publish data you'd be comfortable seeing on a public web page.`,
        visual: {
          type: "diagram",
          svg: `<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 1100 1100"><rect width="1100" height="1100" fill="#1a1a2e"/><text x="550" y="60" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffd700" font-size="32" font-weight="bold">Surface Decision Matrix</text><rect x="60" y="120" width="1000" height="50" fill="#888"/><text x="200" y="153" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffffff" font-size="18" font-weight="bold">Audience</text><text x="500" y="153" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffffff" font-size="18" font-weight="bold">Surface</text><text x="850" y="153" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffffff" font-size="18" font-weight="bold">License</text><rect x="60" y="170" width="1000" height="80" fill="#6366f1" opacity="0.3"/><text x="200" y="217" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffffff" font-size="16">Internal employees</text><text x="500" y="217" text-anchor="middle" fill="#10b981" font-size="16">Service + App</text><text x="850" y="217" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffffff" font-size="16">Pro per user</text><rect x="60" y="250" width="1000" height="80" fill="#6366f1" opacity="0.3"/><text x="200" y="297" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffffff" font-size="16">Branded internal portal</text><text x="500" y="297" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffd700" font-size="16">User Owns Embed</text><text x="850" y="297" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffffff" font-size="16">Pro per user</text><rect x="60" y="330" width="1000" height="80" fill="#6366f1" opacity="0.3"/><text x="200" y="377" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffffff" font-size="16">External SaaS customers</text><text x="500" y="377" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ec4899" font-size="16">App Owns Embed</text><text x="850" y="377" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffffff" font-size="16">F-SKU / A-SKU</text><rect x="60" y="410" width="1000" height="80" fill="#6366f1" opacity="0.3"/><text x="200" y="457" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffffff" font-size="16">Field staff on phones</text><text x="500" y="457" text-anchor="middle" fill="#0ea5e9" font-size="16">Mobile + alerts</text><text x="850" y="457" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffffff" font-size="16">Pro per user</text><rect x="60" y="490" width="1000" height="80" fill="#6366f1" opacity="0.3"/><text x="200" y="537" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffffff" font-size="16">Public anonymous</text><text x="500" y="537" text-anchor="middle" fill="#f59e0b" font-size="16">Publish to web</text><text x="850" y="537" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ef4444" font-size="16">No RLS!</text><rect x="80" y="580" width="940" height="220" fill="#ef4444" rx="12" opacity="0.25"/><text x="550" y="630" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ef4444" font-size="26" font-weight="bold">Embed Limitations to Know</text><text x="140" y="685" fill="#ffffff" font-size="20">- Q&amp;A natural-language: limited support in embed</text><text x="140" y="730" fill="#ffffff" font-size="20">- Smart Narratives: not fully available embedded</text><text x="140" y="775" fill="#ffffff" font-size="20">- RLS: STILL enforced (and required for SaaS)</text><rect x="100" y="830" width="900" height="230" fill="#ffd700" rx="12" opacity="0.2"/><text x="550" y="880" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffd700" font-size="26" font-weight="bold">Final Rule</text><text x="550" y="940" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffffff" font-size="22">Start with the SIMPLEST surface that works.</text><text x="550" y="985" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffffff" font-size="22">Browser-share via App handles 80% of cases.</text><text x="550" y="1030" text-anchor="middle" fill="#10b981" font-size="22" font-weight="bold">Embed only when you truly need custom chrome.</text></svg>`,
          caption: "Match surface to audience — and start with the simplest one (browser + App) that meets the need."
        }
      }
